From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: where the guest's pointer goes over another display's window, tested without AppKit

What: a header with no AppKit in it: the place and size of the guest's
pointer image over the window of an output other than the main one, from
the cursor plane's top left and the image's size in the output's pixels,
stretched as that window stretches the output's frames (each axis on its
own); hidden while a size is unknown or the image lies wholly off the
output. Used by omacvm-cocoa-pointer-heads.patch (which explains the why).

Why its own file: so the rules are tested without QEMU or a window
(app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-heads.sh applies this patch to an
empty folder; at build time and in CI).

Upstream: with omacvm-cocoa-pointer-heads.patch; not sent.
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-heads.c.

--- a/ui/omacvm-pointer-heads.h
+++ b/ui/omacvm-pointer-heads.h
@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+/*
+ * OmacVM: the guest's pointer over the windows of the other displays
+ * (#554, ADR 0054).
+ *
+ * No AppKit in here, so it is tested on its own
+ * (app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-heads.c); ui/cocoa.m uses it.
+ *
+ * With the switch "Pointer on its own layer" every output of the guest has
+ * a cursor plane (its virtio-gpu driver with cursor_plane=1) and the guest
+ * draws no pointer into its frames. QEMU shows each plane's image as a
+ * layer over the window of that output: the main window's cursor layer,
+ * and one over each window of the other displays. The plane's position is
+ * the image's top left in the output's pixels. Those windows show the
+ * output's frames stretched over the whole view, each axis on its own, so
+ * the image is placed and sized the same way.
+ */
+#ifndef OMACVM_POINTER_HEADS_H
+#define OMACVM_POINTER_HEADS_H
+
+#include <stdbool.h>
+
+typedef struct OmacVMHeadPointerFrame {
+    bool shown;
+    double x, y;    /* the image's top left, view points from the bottom left */
+    double w, h;    /* its size, view points */
+} OmacVMHeadPointerFrame;
+
+/*
+ * on: the guest shows the plane; (x, y): its top left and cw x ch its size,
+ * guest pixels of an ow x oh output; vw x vh: the view, points. Not shown
+ * while any size is unknown or the image lies wholly off the output (the
+ * guest moved it to another one). x and y come from the guest: any value.
+ */
+static inline OmacVMHeadPointerFrame
+omacvm_head_pointer_frame(bool on, int x, int y, int cw, int ch,
+                          int ow, int oh, double vw, double vh)
+{
+    OmacVMHeadPointerFrame f = { false, 0, 0, 0, 0 };
+    double sx, sy;
+
+    if (!on || cw <= 0 || ch <= 0 || ow <= 0 || oh <= 0 || !(vw > 0) || !(vh > 0)) {
+        return f;
+    }
+    if (x >= ow || y >= oh || x <= -cw || y <= -ch) {
+        return f;
+    }
+    sx = vw / ow;
+    sy = vh / oh;
+    f.shown = true;
+    f.x = x * sx;
+    f.y = vh - y * sy;
+    f.w = cw * sx;
+    f.h = ch * sy;
+    return f;
+}
+
+#endif /* OMACVM_POINTER_HEADS_H */
